.TH AVR\-PR\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.3.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-pr-list \- List pull requests across repositories.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr pr list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List pull requests across repositories.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr pr list
    avr pr list --scope authored
    avr pr list --repo acme/widgets --state merged
    avr pr list --json number,title,mergeability
    avr pr list --json '?'           # list available fields
    avr pr list --json '*'           # all fields
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    author_login, base_ref, base_sha, check_status, comment_count, created_at,
    draft, head_ref, head_sha, mergeability, merged, number, repository_full_name,
    repository_id, state, title, unresolved_thread_count, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Pass --repo more than once to filter multiple repositories. Auto-detected from git remote if omitted. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fICHOICE\fR
List every readable PR, PRs you authored, or PRs you are involved in. (choices: all, authored, involved; default: all)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by pull request state. 'all' removes the state filter. (choices: open, closed, merged, all; default: open)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max PRs to return. (default: 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Pagination cursor from a previous response.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-pr (1)
